# DTF tier manifest: conda-proxy-scan-grading  (artifact-keeper#4594, #4600,
# #4582; all 1.11.0, follow-ups to the conda scan-on-proxy gate #4585)
# Profile-set: filesystem + upstreams.mock-conda-scan (a stdlib http.server
# conda channel the oracle fills with host-built packages via docker cp).
# LOCAL-ONLY: verdicts come from the backend image's bundled Grype and its
# pre-seeded vulnerability DB; no scanner sidecar, no OSV, no internet.
#
# THE FIXES
# #4594  a fail_closed conda Remote locked (423) every package the scanner ran
#        over to completion and cataloged nothing for (data packages such as
#        tzdata). Now: `clean`, graded on contents, stored with
#        components_cataloged = 0 and reused.
# #4600  a package the scanner catalogs only under a vendored upstream name
#        (libzlib cataloged as zlib) failed the identity check and stayed
#        inconclusive. Now: graded on its findings (clean or vulnerable), stored
#        with the count of what was cataloged.
# #4582  the dashboard's policy_violations_blocked counted proxied content with
#        a blocking verdict on a format that does not run the gate (generic,
#        rpm, go...). Now: only digests a gated format's Remote refuses.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.10.0 (no conda gate at all: every package streams 200
# with no X-AK-Scan, no verdict row, the counter ignores proxy verdicts).
# Green: ak-backend:1.11.0 and newer.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: one admin login then ~30 calls back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock sits on a private per-slot subnet.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-conda-scan"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
